      "detail": "Northumbria Police — summary for the family, via the coroner’s officer. A Maritime and Coastguard Agency investigation is ongoing.\n\nSunday 28 September 2025. Ebba Belle (Dunn’s Boats, Seahouses): the last public sailing of the season from St Ebba’s Isle.\n16:09–16:31 — Forty return e-tickets scanned at the island’s Landing, among them those of Mr T. ASHBY and Mrs N. ASHBY (39). The vessel left at 16:34 and made the skipper’s customary last-day loop around the north end of the island.\n17:08 — At Seahouses the skipper, Mr R. DUNN, counted thirty-nine passengers ashore. Mrs ASHBY could not be found. 17:12 — Coastguard alerted. Lifeboat and helicopter searched the route and the north end until dark.\nMonday 29 September, 07:50 — Mrs ASHBY’s body recovered by the lifeboat from the sea below the cliffs at the north end of the island.\n\nPost-mortem (initial): drowning. A wound above the right temple from a blow against a hard edge, consistent with the vessel’s hull or rocks. Grazes to both palms. No alcohol or drugs.\n\nMrs ASHBY last communicated at 16:22, when she messaged her husband to board and save her a seat. Her ticket was scanned at 16:26. Her phone has not been recovered. She was wearing a yellow waterproof jacket. No passenger recalls seeing her on board. It is believed she went up to the open upper deck for the north-end loop, in a heavy swell, and fell overboard unseen. The upper-deck rail is 1.0 m high.\n\nNo suspicion of third-party involvement. The MCA is examining the operator’s procedure for counting persons on board, and the upper deck. Mr DUNN’s boatmaster’s licence is suspended pending the investigation. Inquest opened and adjourned."
